A||N||11||Gasolene||fiero cooling system||||1||
Z||000000||Gasolene||03-28-2001||02:46 PM||||84 fiero 2m4, 2.5L, 4spd<P>I have a very slow leak in my cooling system.  I've just been filling the reserv once a month and so far that works fine.  However, my radiator doesn't get hot, even after 1 hour of driving.  my temp gage is always in the middle.<P>I can't find the leak because it is so slow.<P>Is there a danger of overheating if the radiator doesn't get hot or build up pressure?||||reg||1
Z||000001||fyerstarter||03-28-2001||07:34 PM||||I have the same problem with my car. I have located the leak though , its in one of the metal cooling lines that run under the car but is so slow I can only tell if I let the car sit for a few days in the same spot. Anyway if your temp gauge is working and it is not reading hot then you shouldnt have anything to worry about. As long as you keep the proper amount of coolant in your system.<P>If your car is runnning extremely cool you think for your climate then you may want to check the thermostat. Possibly its stuck open..||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||03-29-2001||12:16 AM||||Also, pay close attention to how the car behaves.  I've had a car overheat and warp the head and the temp guage never read hot.  The guage worked fine, but there was an air pocket at the temp sensor, so it wasn't reading the correct coolant temp!  Be careful!||||reg||4
Z||000003||Gasolene||03-29-2001||12:41 AM||||how does a car behave if it is overheating??<BR>is there any other way to check besides the temp gauge??||||reg||1
Z||000004||fyerstarter||03-29-2001||01:39 AM||||One sign that it's getting too hot is when you come to a stop it will stall. Also of course watch for steam coming from under the hood as the pressure will sometimes blow the cap off the overflow bottle...and you'll usually smell coolant||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gasolene||03-29-2001||03:45 PM||||it doesn't stall, it runs fine as far as I can tell.  There is no pressure built up, so I don't see any steam, but I do smell coolent when I drive.||||reg||1
Z||000006||286SE'S||03-29-2001||03:51 PM||||Smelling coolant when you drive usually indicates a leaky heater core. I had that<BR>problem and it took a while before it actually started dripping onto the passenger side carpet. You can remove the cover plate near the 'blue dingy thingy' and see if there is antifreeze residue at the bottom of the core.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gasolene||03-29-2001||08:20 PM||||when I bought the car, there was a stain on the rug.  but it hasn't been wet since I've had the car.<P>if it is the heater core, do I need to replace it, or is it fixable?||||reg||1
Z||000008||MikeSchaefer||03-29-2001||09:03 PM||||I found on my car that a leak was caused by the previous owner trying to screw something onto the core.  I replaced the electrical tape that I used to cover the hole once a year and it was fine,  try that, no one will know but you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Mike||||reg||2
Z||000009||WKDFIRO||03-30-2001||04:53 AM||||If its small enough than it can just be spot welded and you can be on your marry way. <P>It can be replaced but I haven't had to price one in a long time. Im pretty sure that any radiator place can preasure test the core and find out if its leaking.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000010||Gasolene||03-30-2001||06:59 PM||||Also, I sometimes see drips of antifreez under my car (above the rad) If I leave it overnight.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Gasolene (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||03-30-2001||09:36 PM||||If it's the heater core just replace it. Once they start leaking in one spot some other spot isn't far behind after a fix.<P>If it's not building pressure something is wrong. plane and simple. This needs to be fixed.<P>You need to rent/borrow/build a pressure tester for the cooling system and bring it up to at least 13-15PSI. then get under it and see where the drip is.<P>Another issue is that the lack of pressure is causing wear in the water pump. Don't be suprised if it croaks once the leak is fixed. (I know it sounds weird... The pump needs that pressure to work right.)||||reg||1
